**Cause:** In `Collector.delete()` (django/db/models/deletion.py), the fast path for a single object with no dependencies — the "Optimize for the case with a single obj and no dependencies" branch — returned early with `return count, {model._meta.label: count}`, skipping the PK-clearing loop at the end of the method. So deleting a dependency-free instance left its PK set, unlike the general path which sets `instance.<pk>.attname = None` for every collected instance.

**Fix (minimal, 1 line, source only — no test changes, nothing committed):**
```python
# line 280, in the fast-delete branch, after delete_batch:
setattr(instance, model._meta.pk.attname, None)
```

